    "body": "Hey Carl!\r\n\r\nIf you take a look at the `package.json` in the `/docs` directory, you can see the list of existing scripts available (`dev` and `build`). `npx` _would_ work, but it is not the usual way to get your local environment up and running, and may not trigger the needed pre/post install hooks when setting up your development environment. Right now there are no hooks in place yet, but it's just something worth keeping in mind.\r\n\r\nHere are my suggested setup steps.\r\n\r\n### Setup \r\n1. `cd` into the `/docs` directory.\r\n1. Install the project dependencies:\r\n```sh\r\nnpm install\r\n```\r\n1. Start the project in development mode:\r\n```\r\nnpm run dev\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think that `CONTRIBUTING.md` would be a great place to put these docs, if you are interested in documenting how to get the docs site running locally! 😄 ",
